{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/913499-advice-on-handling-knowledge-skils-for-a-new-st","id":913499,"title":"Advice on handling knowledge skils for a new ST?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-13T10:43:52-07:00","id":913499,"title":"Advice on handling knowledge skils for a new ST?","content":"I'm running a blended innocents/hunter game. My issue is that, as a new ST, I'm not entirely sure how to handle knowledge skills like occult in a way that rewards players for taking them, but doesn't take away the mystery of the game. I'm more used to D&amp;D where knowledge skills pretty much give you the statblock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4777-warkitty","name":"WarKitty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T11:45:01-07:00","id":913551,"title":"","content":"Have you got <b>Chronicles of Darkness Rulebook</b>? It has nice spread of Skills and usage of them in play. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T11:50:22-07:00","id":913554,"title":"","content":"Yes I do, I was just hoping for something a little more in-depth than just what's in the rulebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4777-warkitty","name":"WarKitty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T14:37:31-07:00","id":913661,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4777-warkitty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4777\" data-vbnamecard=\"4777\">WarKitty</a><br /> <br /> This is a quote from a post where I share how I run perception/knowledge rolls for NPCs<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/910711-cabal-at-war-the-power-of-mages-report-from-the-last-game-session?p=913628#post913628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Things like this is why I normally roll behind a screen a few times during a scene whether I need to or not (the roll which I don't actually track for success acts as a placeholder for rolls I may think up as having been appropriate reflexive perception or knowledge rolls I'll make between games when planning how much info the antagonists have). I think it is more fair that merely arbitrating based on my common sense, and maintains the illusion I as storyteller am smart enough to think of every applicable roll instantaneously. I like my worlds very sandbox and with balanced arbitration via rules and die rolls rather than railroading plot details via the magic wand of plot-tonium.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I handle successes as pieces of information, with several different facts for any situation.<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> Occult would reveal a series of conflicting information about vampires, and for a success I would reveal that to the player making the roll. I'd let them know Bram Stokers Dracula actually was original fiction that only borrowed loosely from actual myths. In old European legends about blood thirsty revenants rising from their grave and returning at dawn, the corpse is animated by an evil spirit which can flee in the form of vermin swarms if the body is destroyed and that is why bodies were staked. Also that isn't the only type of vampire and comparing traits in the field versus research is the best way to figure out which it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-13-2016, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}